5. What is a Web Server?

A web server is a software or hardware that delivers web pages to users over the internet using HTTP.
It stores, processes, and serves website files to browsers when requested.

Examples:

Apache HTTP Server

Nginx

Microsoft IIS

Node.js (Express)

LiteSpeed

