8. Static vs Dynamic Websites
Type	Description	Example
Static Website	Shows the same content to every user; built using HTML, CSS only.	A personal portfolio website or company info page.
Dynamic Website	Displays data that changes based on user input or database; uses backend languages.	Facebook, Amazon, YouTube.
9. Five Popular Web Browsers & Rendering Engines
Browser	Rendering Engine	Description
Google Chrome	Blink	Fast, modern engine used by most browsers.
Mozilla Firefox	Gecko	Open-source engine known for standards compliance.
Microsoft Edge	Blink	Uses the same engine as Chrome (since 2020).
Apple Safari	WebKit	Optimized for Apple devices.
Opera	Blink	Built on Chromium with additional features like VPN.

Rendering engines differ in how they parse HTML/CSS, handle JavaScript, and optimize layouts, which can slightly change how a site appears across browsers.

